    "goal": "Size a PLINK binary genotype dataset: report the full .bed size and per-chromosome .bed size for a GWAS cohort of 3467 samples and 7,757,616 variants (514,742 on the largest chromosome).",
    "rationale": "The .bed binary format packs 2 bits per sample per variant (4 samples/byte). Full dataset size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB; per-chromosome size uses the largest chromosome's variant count. The number of per-chromosome files equals the number of chromosomes in the dataset, estimated from the variant distribution (total ÷ largest-chromosome variants ≈ 15).",
